PAGES = {
 'en': dict(
  src='dj-multicam-editing/index.html', out=f'{SLUG}/index.html', url=f'{ORIGIN}/{SLUG}/', home='/', p='',
  title='Sync Multicam Footage to Music in Premiere Pro | Auto Audio Sync',
  desc='Sync every camera clip to the master music in Premiere Pro automatically. Each clip is placed by its own audio and camera clock, ready for AI multicam editing.',
  ogdesc='Line up every camera clip to the master mix in Adobe Premiere Pro, then let the music drive the multicam edit.',
  crumb='Sync multicam to music',
  headline='Sync multicam footage to the master music in Adobe Premiere Pro',
  body='''<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Multicam AI</a><span> / Sync multicam to music</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">NEW IN v2.3.11.6 · BETA · LIFETIME LICENSE</p><h1>Sync multicam footage to the master music in Premiere Pro</h1><p class="subtle">By Rizki Ardiansyah, creator of R Project Multicam AI · Updated 16 October 2026</p><p class="lead">Before any camera can switch on the beat, every clip has to sit at the right moment against the music. Sync to Master Music lines up all of your camera clips to the master mix on A1 automatically, so you can go straight to music-driven multicam editing.</p><!--rp:toc--><!--/rp:toc--><h2 id="what-sync-to-master-music-does">What Sync to Master Music does</h2><p>Live events rarely give you one continuous file per camera. Cameras are stopped and restarted, phones record short clips and batteries are swapped mid-set. Lining those clips up by hand against a long DJ mix can take hours.</p><p>Sync to Master Music reads the master music on A1, listens to each camera clip's own audio and places the clip where it belongs on the timeline. It also uses the camera clock to keep clips from the same camera in the right order. The result is a <strong>new synced sequence</strong>; your current sequence is not changed.</p><h2 id="when-to-use-it">When to use it</h2><ul><li><strong>DJ sets and club nights:</strong> several cameras with many start/stop clips and one clean master recording from the mixer.</li><li><strong>Concerts and festivals:</strong> stage, crowd and handheld angles recorded separately from the board mix.</li><li><strong>Short clips:</strong> very short clips are placed too; clips that are too short or too unclear to place reliably go to Review instead of stopping the job.</li></ul><h2 id="how-confidence-and-review-work">How confidence and review work</h2><p>Every placement gets a confidence check. Clips the engine is sure about are placed directly. Medium-confidence clips are labelled <strong>[CHECK]</strong> so you can jump to them and confirm the position in a few seconds. Clips it is unsure about are put on a <strong>muted Review track</strong>, so nothing questionable ends up in the edit without you seeing it.</p><h2 id="step-by-step-in-premiere-pro">Step by step in Premiere Pro</h2><ol><li>Place the master music or the mixer recording on A1 of a sequence.</li><li>Import the camera clips you want to sync into the project.</li><li>Open the Multicam AI panel and choose <strong>Sync to Master Music · Beta</strong>.</li><li>Run the sync and open the new synced sequence it builds.</li><li>Check the clips marked [CHECK] and the muted Review track, then continue with <a href="/dj-multicam-editing/">music-driven multicam editing</a>.</li></ol><h2 id="tips-for-the-best-result">Tips for the best result</h2><ul><li>Record camera audio for every angle, even if you will not use it in the final mix: the camera audio is what the sync listens to.</li><li>Use the cleanest master you have, ideally a direct recording from the mixer.</li><li>Set the camera clocks before the event; it helps keep clips from one camera in order.</li><li>Keep a backup of your project before working on a long set, and review the synced sequence before you start cutting.</li></ul><section id="sync-questions"><h2 id="sync-questions-title">Sync to Master Music questions</h2><h3>Does Sync to Master Music change my original sequence?</h3><p>No. It builds a new synced sequence and leaves your current sequence as it is.</p><h3>Which license do I need?</h3><p>Sync to Master Music is included with the lifetime license. It is a beta feature in plugin v2.3.11.6 and newer.</p><h3>What happens to clips that cannot be matched?</h3><p>Clips the engine is unsure about are placed on a muted Review track, and medium-confidence clips are labelled [CHECK]. Nothing is deleted.</p><h3>Do I still need to review the result?</h3><p>Yes. This is a beta feature: check the [CHECK] clips and the Review track before you edit. Camera audio quality, crowd noise and very short clips affect how reliably a clip can be placed.</p></section><h2 id="next-let-the-music-drive-the-cut">Next: let the music drive the cut</h2><p>Once the cameras are in sync, analyze the music and let the camera plan follow beats, phrases and drops. Camera Roles keep the edit varied: two angles of the same kind, such as wide after wide, never follow each other. See the <a href="/ai-multicam-editor-premiere-pro/">AI multicam editor for Premiere Pro</a> and the <a href="/guides/music-driven-multicam-editing/">music-driven editing guide</a>.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/#pricing">Get lifetime access</a><a class="button secondary" href="/#downloads">Download Multicam AI</a></div><nav class="actions" aria-label="Related resources"><a href="/dj-multicam-editing/">DJ multicam editing</a><a href="/guides/install-multicam-ai/">Installation guide</a><a href="/help/">Troubleshooting</a><a href="/releases/">Release notes</a></nav>''',
  faq=[('Does Sync to Master Music change my original sequence?','No. It builds a new synced sequence and leaves your current sequence as it is.'),
       ('Which license do I need?','Sync to Master Music is included with the lifetime license. It is a beta feature in plugin v2.3.11.6 and newer.'),
       ('What happens to clips that cannot be matched?','Clips the engine is unsure about are placed on a muted Review track, and medium-confidence clips are labelled [CHECK]. Nothing is deleted.'),
       ('Do I still need to review the result?','Yes. This is a beta feature: check the [CHECK] clips and the Review track before you edit.')]),
 'id': dict(
  src='id/dj-multicam-editing/index.html', out=f'id/{SLUG}/index.html', url=f'{ORIGIN}/id/{SLUG}/', home='/id/', p='/id',
  title='Sinkron Footage Multicam ke Musik di Premiere Pro | Auto Sync Audio',
  desc='Sinkronkan semua klip kamera ke musik master di Premiere Pro secara otomatis. Tiap klip ditempatkan lewat audionya sendiri dan jam kamera, siap untuk edit multicam AI.',
  ogdesc='Selaraskan semua klip kamera ke musik master di Adobe Premiere Pro, lalu biarkan musik memandu edit multicam.',
  crumb='Sinkron multicam ke musik',
  headline='Sinkronkan footage multicam ke musik master di Adobe Premiere Pro',
  body='''<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/id/">Multicam AI</a><span> / Sinkron multicam ke musik</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">BARU DI v2.3.11.6 · BETA · LISENSI LIFETIME</p><h1>Sinkronkan footage multicam ke musik master di Premiere Pro</h1><p class="subtle">Oleh Rizki Ardiansyah, pembuat R Project Multicam AI · Diperbarui 16 Oktober 2026</p><p class="lead">Sebelum kamera bisa berganti mengikuti beat, setiap klip harus berada di momen yang tepat terhadap musiknya. Sync to Master Music menyelaraskan semua klip kamera ke musik master di A1 secara otomatis, jadi kamu bisa langsung lanjut ke edit multicam yang mengikuti musik.</p><!--rp:toc--><!--/rp:toc--><h2 id="what-sync-to-master-music-does">Apa yang dilakukan Sync to Master Music</h2><p>Acara live jarang menghasilkan satu file utuh per kamera. Kamera dimatikan lalu dinyalakan lagi, HP merekam klip pendek, dan baterai diganti di tengah set. Menyusun klip-klip itu secara manual terhadap mix DJ yang panjang bisa memakan waktu berjam-jam.</p><p>Sync to Master Music membaca musik master di A1, mendengarkan audio dari setiap klip kamera, lalu menempatkan klip itu di posisinya di timeline. Jam kamera juga dipakai agar klip dari kamera yang sama tetap berurutan. Hasilnya adalah <strong>sequence baru yang sudah sinkron</strong>; sequence-mu yang sekarang tidak diubah.</p><h2 id="when-to-use-it">Kapan memakainya</h2><ul><li><strong>DJ set dan club night:</strong> beberapa kamera dengan banyak klip start/stop dan satu rekaman master bersih dari mixer.</li><li><strong>Konser dan festival:</strong> angle panggung, crowd dan handheld yang direkam terpisah dari mix board.</li><li><strong>Klip pendek:</strong> klip yang sangat pendek juga ditempatkan; klip yang terlalu pendek atau kurang jelas untuk ditempatkan dengan yakin masuk ke Review tanpa menghentikan proses.</li></ul><h2 id="how-confidence-and-review-work">Cara kerja tingkat keyakinan dan review</h2><p>Setiap penempatan dicek tingkat keyakinannya. Klip yang sudah pasti langsung ditempatkan. Klip dengan keyakinan sedang diberi label <strong>[CHECK]</strong> supaya kamu bisa langsung melompat ke sana dan memastikan posisinya dalam beberapa detik. Klip yang belum pasti diletakkan di <strong>track Review yang di-mute</strong>, jadi tidak ada yang meragukan masuk ke edit tanpa kamu lihat.</p><h2 id="step-by-step-in-premiere-pro">Langkah demi langkah di Premiere Pro</h2><ol><li>Letakkan musik master atau rekaman mixer di A1 sebuah sequence.</li><li>Import klip kamera yang ingin disinkronkan ke dalam project.</li><li>Buka panel Multicam AI dan pilih <strong>Sync to Master Music · Beta</strong>.</li><li>Jalankan sinkronisasi lalu buka sequence baru yang dibuatnya.</li><li>Cek klip berlabel [CHECK] dan track Review yang di-mute, lalu lanjutkan ke <a href="/id/dj-multicam-editing/">edit multicam yang mengikuti musik</a>.</li></ol><h2 id="tips-for-the-best-result">Tips agar hasilnya maksimal</h2><ul><li>Rekam audio kamera di setiap angle, walaupun tidak dipakai di mix akhir: audio kamera itulah yang didengarkan oleh proses sinkron.</li><li>Pakai master paling bersih yang kamu punya, idealnya rekaman langsung dari mixer.</li><li>Atur jam kamera sebelum acara; ini membantu menjaga urutan klip dari satu kamera.</li><li>Simpan backup project sebelum mengerjakan set panjang, dan review sequence hasil sinkron sebelum mulai memotong.</li></ul><section id="sync-questions"><h2 id="sync-questions-title">Pertanyaan seputar Sync to Master Music</h2><h3>Apakah Sync to Master Music mengubah sequence asli saya?</h3><p>Tidak. Fitur ini membuat sequence baru yang sudah sinkron dan membiarkan sequence-mu yang sekarang apa adanya.</p><h3>Lisensi apa yang saya butuhkan?</h3><p>Sync to Master Music termasuk dalam lisensi lifetime. Ini fitur beta di plugin v2.3.11.6 ke atas.</p><h3>Bagaimana dengan klip yang tidak bisa dicocokkan?</h3><p>Klip yang belum pasti diletakkan di track Review yang di-mute, dan klip dengan keyakinan sedang diberi label [CHECK]. Tidak ada yang dihapus.</p><h3>Apakah saya tetap perlu me-review hasilnya?</h3><p>Ya. Ini fitur beta: cek klip [CHECK] dan track Review sebelum mulai mengedit. Kualitas audio kamera, suara crowd dan klip yang sangat pendek memengaruhi seberapa yakin sebuah klip bisa ditempatkan.</p></section><h2 id="next-let-the-music-drive-the-cut">Berikutnya: biarkan musik memandu cut</h2><p>Setelah kamera sinkron, analisis musiknya dan biarkan rencana kamera mengikuti beat, frasa dan drop. Camera Roles menjaga edit tetap bervariasi: dua angle dengan jenis yang sama, misalnya wide setelah wide, tidak akan berurutan. Lihat <a href="/id/ai-multicam-editor-premiere-pro/">editor multicam AI untuk Premiere Pro</a> dan <a href="/id/guides/music-driven-multicam-editing/">panduan editing berbasis musik</a>.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/id/#pricing">Dapatkan akses lifetime</a><a class="button secondary" href="/id/#downloads">Download Multicam AI</a></div><nav class="actions" aria-label="Sumber terkait"><a href="/id/dj-multicam-editing/">Edit multicam DJ</a><a href="/id/guides/install-multicam-ai/">Panduan instalasi</a><a href="/id/help/">Troubleshooting</a><a href="/id/releases/">Catatan rilis</a></nav>''',
  faq=[('Apakah Sync to Master Music mengubah sequence asli saya?','Tidak. Fitur ini membuat sequence baru yang sudah sinkron dan membiarkan sequence-mu yang sekarang apa adanya.'),
       ('Lisensi apa yang saya butuhkan?','Sync to Master Music termasuk dalam lisensi lifetime. Ini fitur beta di plugin v2.3.11.6 ke atas.'),
       ('Bagaimana dengan klip yang tidak bisa dicocokkan?','Klip yang belum pasti diletakkan di track Review yang di-mute, dan klip dengan keyakinan sedang diberi label [CHECK]. Tidak ada yang dihapus.'),
       ('Apakah saya tetap perlu me-review hasilnya?','Ya. Ini fitur beta: cek klip [CHECK] dan track Review sebelum mulai mengedit.')]),
}

for lang, c in PAGES.items():
    s = (SITE / c['src']).read_text(encoding='utf-8')
    s = re.sub(r'<title>.*?</title>', f'<title>{c["title"]}</title>', s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<meta name="description" content=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['desc'], s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<link rel="canonical" href=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['url'], s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<meta property="og:title" content=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['title'], s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<meta name="twitter:title" content=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['title'], s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<meta property="og:description" content=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['ogdesc'], s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<meta name="twitter:description" content=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['ogdesc'], s, count=1)
    s = re.sub(r'(<meta property="og:url" content=")[^"]*', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['url'], s, count=1)
    ld = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [
        {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [
            {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "R Project Multicam AI", "item": ORIGIN + c['home']},
            {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": c['crumb'], "item": c['url']}]},
        {"@type": "TechArticle", "headline": c['headline'], "description": c['desc'], "url": c['url'], "inLanguage": lang,
         "dateModified": DATE, "author": {"@type": "Person", "name": "Rizki Ardiansyah", "url": ORIGIN + '/'},
         "publisher": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "R Project", "url": ORIGIN + '/'},
         "image": ORIGIN + "/social-preview.png", "mainEntityOfPage": c['url']},
        {"@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": q, "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": a}} for q, a in c['faq']]}]}
    s = re.sub(r'<script type="application/ld\+json">.*?</script>',
               lambda m: '<script type="application/ld+json">' + json.dumps(ld, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')) + '</script>', s, count=1, flags=re.S)
    s = re.sub(r'(<main id="main" class="wrap section guide-content">).*?(</main>)', lambda m: m.group(1) + c['body'] + m.group(2), s, count=1, flags=re.S)
    out = SITE / c['out']
    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    out.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')
    print('wrote', out.relative_to(ROOT))
